# Bytecode cache
__pycache__/

# Graphify knowledge graph. ALLOWLIST: ignore everything graphify writes into
# graphify-out/, then re-include only the portable snapshot that CLAUDE.md's
# graphify rule commits once per phase on this branch. A denylist kept missing
# new outputs (.graphify_labels.json, .graphify_python, dated YYYY-MM-DD/ dumps).
#
# Why those three stay tracked (measured 2026-09-13): a fresh checkout WITH
# graph.json regenerates in ~40s and keeps the 315 LLM-derived ("semantic")
# nodes; WITHOUT it, `graphify update .` rebuilds code-only and every semantic
# node is lost until a paid LLM pass. History cost of tracking is ~1.4 MB packed.
#
# Keep the `graphify-out/*` form: a directory-level `graphify-out/` ignore
# cannot be negated and would silently ignore graph.json as well.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/graph.json
!graphify-out/manifest.json
!graphify-out/.graphify_analysis.json
# byte-identical duplicate of graphify-out/graph.json
.planning/graphs/

# insta snapshot scratch (47-CONTEXT.md D-14). `*.snap.new` is what insta writes
# beside a baseline when a snapshot is missing or mismatches under its local
# default mode — transient, never reviewed, never committed. `*.snap` itself
# stays TRACKED on purpose: the committed baseline IS the reviewable artifact,
# so every prompt wording change must appear in the PR diff. Never widen this
# rule to cover the baselines.
*.snap.new

# External-review raw traces (regenerable, hundreds of KB each)
.planning/phases/**/codex.err
.planning/phases/**/codex.clean
.planning/phases/**/agy.err
